{"name":"Picket Fence","hex":"#f3f2ea","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"picket fence","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A simple fence made from wooden pickets, connected by horizontal bars.","A series of spaced perpendicular striations that occasionally occur in aurorae."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/picket_fence"}],"entries":[{"title":"Picket fence","blocks":[{"text":"Picket fences are a type of fence often used decoratively for domestic boundaries, distinguished by their evenly spaced vertical boards, the pickets, attached to horizontal rails. Picket fences are particularly popular in the United States, with the white picket fence coming to symbolize the ideal middle-class suburban life."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Classic_Picket_Fence.JPG/330px-Classic_Picket_Fence.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picket_fence","wikidata":"Q3487546"},{"title":"Fence","blocks":[{"text":"A fence is a structure that encloses an area, typically outdoors creating a boundary, and is usually constructed from posts that are connected by boards, wire, rails or netting. A fence differs from a wall in not having a solid foundation along its whole length."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a2/Westtown.jpg/330px-Westtown.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fence","wikidata":"Q148571"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/OrazioneOrtoBotticelli.jpg/500px-OrazioneOrtoBotticelli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/OrazioneOrtoBotticelli.jpg/500px-OrazioneOrtoBotticelli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Painting with a picket fen